think Surveyed the Mycelium consensus stack (Cord · Voucher · Chorus · Muster · Warrant · Constel …). The honest blind spot: Constel reaches quorum IN one process (reach_quorum returns a head and nothing else); nothing carries the constellation's belief OUT as a portable, offline-verifiable artifact.
think Checked chorus_bron — it already lets a bare Chorus travel and re-verify at a STATED threshold, no Dag. Its weakness: it carries no roster, so it cannot tell an enrolled ship from a stranger with a valid signature. That is exactly the gap a NAMED constellation closes.
think Named the crux: a Testament — a certificate carrying the roster NAMES + the sealed Chorus. A recipient boots the exact roster from the names alone (Constel's reproducible gift), seats the Muster, derives the Byzantine threshold from the roster size, and passes the seal offline. Genuinely stronger than a bare travelling Chorus and non-duplicative.
think Confirmed name freedom: testament/ratify/docket/beacon all zero collisions; the existing "certificate" language belongs to warrant (roll-rotation), a different thing. Chose Testament (warm, clear, safe per the Comlink tendency).
think Read chorus/muster/voucher structs and confirmed verify_voucher · verify_chorus · pass_muster all work with NO Dag — so a seal made WITH the ledger verifies WITHOUT it. Designed seal_subset (first k ships) so full-seal, thin-quorum, and r2's f-down all share one path (DRY).
obs Teeth chosen to prove the named binding a bare Chorus cannot: (1) a stranger's valid, agreeing voucher refuses NotMember; (2) a thin quorum below the DERIVED threshold refuses BelowQuorum; (3) a one-byte name tamper re-boots a different key so the real signer stops being a member → NotMember, proving binding to the exact names byte for byte.
obs Self-approved the design round (exploration doc first) and landed r1 in the same turn rather than checking in — the itinerary's filling law authorizes exactly this. Only r1 landed; the finishing edge holds (one keystone, one send). r2-r4 (f-down · travels · reads-true) named for later laps.
obs Composed constel + chorus + muster + voucher public API only, editing none; the four modules re-run GREEN at the witness door. Demo ship/keeper seeds only — a served testament reaches the Comlink gate, a real Kumara instance gates #2/#4; no custody crossed.
